      "message": "feat(finish3d): land model - fill closed openings on the drive surface\n\nA 3D Finish option, `fill_openings` (mm, off by default), plans the path\non the model plus horizontal lids over every closed hole or pocket a flat\ndisk of that diameter cannot enter (grey-scale morphological closing of\nthe top-down height field; openings that run out to an edge or would\nspill over a lower rim are never filled). The finish flies over bolt\nholes at their rim instead of diving down their walls, and the path\nsays what stands as land. Lids are only ever added, so the path can\nrise, never sink; the verifier still judges the real model. Undoable op\nparam, carried by the MCP params door, UI field on the 3D Finish page;\nGeodesic refuses the combination by name. Off is byte-identical (no\ndigest bytes, no file key).\n\nFixes #1196\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
